# Project Overview

## General Guidelines

- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Follow consistent naming conventions
- Write self-documenting code with clear variable and function names
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use meaningful comments for complex business logic

## Code Style

- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Use semicolons
- Use double quotes for strings
- Use trailing commas in multi-line objects and arrays

## Architecture Principles

- Organize code by NestJS modules (one module per domain)
- Keep related files close together (controller, service, DTOs, entities per module)
- Use NestJS dependency injection for better testability
- Implement proper error handling with NestJS exception filters
- Follow single responsibility principle
- Use DTOs for request/response validation
- Use entities for database models
